    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d641">

                <pb facs="0695" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg687"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.60C/114: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Biddle</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Temporarily in France, to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-10T17:00:00+00:00">November 10, 1939—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. I am leaving for Angers<anchor n="32" xml:id="d641-f1"/> accompanied by Mr.
                    and Mrs. Elbrick,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d641-f2"/> Miss McQuatters<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d641-f3"/> and my wife and Moszczynski<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d641-f4"/> on the morning November 12. I signed a lease effective on
                    October 23 for the rental of the Chateau de Plessisboure, on a month to month
                    basis. Inasmuch as the rental charges plus heat and light for this residence
                    property will exceed the maximum allowable to chiefs of mission under the
                    standardized regulations covering rent, heat and light allowances I assume the
                    Department will prefer to grant me the maximum allowable.</p>
                <p>The Elbricks and Miss McQuatters will live at the Hotel Anjou at Angers where I
                    shall establish the Embassy offices for the time being. I recommend that rent
                    allowance and cost of living allowances be granted them on the same basis as
                    officers and clerks in the Paris Embassy.</p>
                <p>I shall submit by pouch estimates for contingent and miscellaneous expenses.</p>
                <pb facs="0696" n="688" xml:id="pg688"/>
                <p>It is believed desirable for the time being to handle telegrams to and from the
                    department through the Paris Embassy which will relay them. I am taking with me
                    to Angers only the Gray Code.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
